m/users/css-meeting-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T16:39:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T16:39:25Z","body":"The CSS Working Group just discussed `[css-values] A few more calc() issues in WPT tests  `, and agreed to the following:\n\n* ``RESOLVED:  remove the `1 * ...` test, and fix the calc-in-MQ test``\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;TabAtkins> weinig: I thin kthe second one has been resolved...<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> weinig: The first one, shoudl `1 * ...` be eliminated?<br>\n&lt;fantasai> TabAtkins: I believe resolution was to not add it, because not very useful simplification<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> weinig: I feel like we resolved on this already?<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> weinig: The last one, I think was just wrong and I was looking for clarification.<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> weinig: But it looks like now everyone is failing it, so i think the test is just wrong<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> weinig: so resolution would be to remove the `1 * ...` test, and fix the calc-in-MQ test<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> changing the tests is fine with me<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> RESOLVED:  remove the `1 * ...` test, and fix the calc-in-MQ test<br>\n</details>\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/5120767200/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]